    "\n",
    "## Learning Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "- Construct document vectors using term counts and TF-IDF.\n",
    "- Calculate next-word probabilities from n-gram counts.\n",
    "- Explain how neural models learn word embeddings.\n",
    "- Distinguish CBOW, Skip-gram, and autoregressive prediction.\n",
    "- Evaluate representation choices for business text analytics.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Lecture Outline\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Text analytics pipeline:** data, preprocessing, and outputs\n",
    "2. **Document representation:** Bag of Words and TF-IDF\n",
    "3. **Language modeling:** sequence probabilities and n-grams\n",
    "4. **Neural representations:** embeddings and Word2Vec\n",
    "5. **Applications:** classification, clustering, and evaluation\n",
    "\n",
    "# Text Analytics Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "## The Core NLP Pipeline\n",
    "\n",
    "```{dot}\n",
    "//| echo: false\n",
    "//| fig-align: center\n",
    "//| fig-alt: \"Core NLP pipeline from raw text to output\"\n",
    "//| file: ./M01_lecture02_figures/m01_core_nlp_pipeline.dot\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Preprocessing** defines the units retained for analysis.\n",
    "- **Representation** determines what information reaches the model.\n",
    "- **Evaluation** measures performance on the intended task.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Structured and Unstructured Business Data\n",
    "\n",
    "| Data type | Examples | Preparation |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Structured | Ratios, returns, filing dates | Validate types, units, and missing values |\n",
    "| Unstructured | Risk factors, MD&A, reviews | Extract text, tokenize, and vectorize |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Unit of analysis:** a filing, section, paragraph, or sentence.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Linking key:** company identifier and reporting period when combining text with financial variables.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
