    "| HTML text extraction | Document text | Section boundaries and boilerplate |\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Preprocessing Decisions\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Tokenization:** define words, subwords, or other analysis units.\n",
    "- **Normalization:** standardize case and whitespace where appropriate.\n",
    "- **Filtering:** retain task-relevant numbers, negation, and terminology.\n",
    "- **Segmentation:** preserve document and sentence boundaries.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Example:** removing “not” changes the interpretation of “revenue did not increase.”\n",
    "\n",
    "# Count-Based Document Representations\n",
    "\n",
    "## Bag of Words: Definition\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.columns}\n",
    "::: {.column width=\"60%\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "For a vocabulary of $V$ terms, represent document $d$ as:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_d = [c_{d1}, c_{d2}, \\ldots, c_{dV}]\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$c_{dj}$ is the count of term $j$ in document $d$.\n",
    "\n",
    "- One feature per vocabulary term\n",
    "- A shared feature order across documents\n",
    "- No encoding of word order within a document\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    "::: {.column width=\"40%\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "![Bag of Words](./M01_lecture02_figures/bag-of-words.png){width=90% fig-alt=\"Words represented as an unordered collection\" #fig-bow}\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    ":::\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Worked Example: Document-Term Matrix\n",
    "\n",
    "- $d_1$: “revenue growth”\n",
    "- $d_2$: “revenue risk”\n",
    "- $d_3$: “risk risk”\n",
    "\n",
    "| Document | growth | revenue | risk |\n",
    "|---|---:|---:|---:|\n",
    "| $d_1$ | 1 | 1 | 0 |\n",
    "| $d_2$ | 0 | 1 | 1 |\n",
    "| $d_3$ | 0 | 0 | 2 |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Matrix shape:** $D \\times V$ = documents × vocabulary terms.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Sparsity:** most entries are zero when each document uses only a small fraction of the vocabulary.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Bag of Words: Uses and Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "| Uses | Limitations |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Interpretable term-level features | Synonyms occupy separate dimensions |\n",
    "| Baseline document classification | A word has the same feature across meanings |\n",
    "| Exact-term retrieval | Word order and syntax are discarded |\n",
    "| Sparse matrix computation | Vocabulary grows with the corpus |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Order loss:** “supplier acquires retailer” and “retailer acquires supplier” have identical unigram counts.\n",
    "\n",
