    "\n",
    "## TF-IDF: Weighting Distinctive Terms\n",
    "\n",
    "Term frequency–inverse document frequency combines within-document counts with corpus-wide rarity:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\operatorname{tfidf}(t,d)=c(t,d)\\operatorname{idf}(t)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "For the smoothed convention used in the next example:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\operatorname{idf}(t)=\\log\\left(\\frac{1+N}{1+\\operatorname{df}(t)}\\right)+1\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- $N$: number of documents\n",
    "- $\\operatorname{df}(t)$: number of documents containing term $t$\n",
    "- Terms occurring in fewer documents receive larger IDF weights.\n",
    "\n",
    "[Source: scikit-learn TF-IDF documentation](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.feature_extraction.text.TfidfTransformer.html)\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Worked Example: TF-IDF Weights\n",
    "\n",
    "Using the three-document corpus:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Term | Document frequency | Smoothed IDF |\n",
    "|---|---:|---:|\n",
    "| growth | 1 | $\\log(4/2)+1 \\approx 1.693$ |\n",
    "| revenue | 2 | $\\log(4/3)+1 \\approx 1.288$ |\n",
    "| risk | 2 | $\\log(4/3)+1 \\approx 1.288$ |\n",
    "\n",
    "For $d_1$ = “revenue growth,” in vocabulary order:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "x_{d_1}=[1.693,\\;1.288,\\;0]\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "With L2 normalization, divide by $\\lVert x_{d_1}\\rVert_2$ to obtain approximately $[0.796,\\;0.605,\\;0]$.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## TF-IDF in Python"
