    "**Interpretation:** values combine counts, IDF, and document normalization; they are not probabilities.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Language Probability and N-grams\n",
    "\n",
    "## Language Modeling: The Chain Rule\n",
    "\n",
    "A language model assigns a probability to a token sequence:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(w_1,\\ldots,w_T)=\\prod_{t=1}^{T}P(w_t\\mid w_1,\\ldots,w_{t-1})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- $w_t$: token at position $t$\n",
    "- $w_{<t}$: all preceding tokens\n",
    "- At each step, the conditional probabilities sum to one over the vocabulary.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Autoregressive generation:** predict a distribution, select a token, append it to the context, and repeat.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## N-gram Language Models\n",
    "\n",
    "Approximate the full history using the previous $n-1$ tokens:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "P(w_t\\mid w_{<t})\\approx P(w_t\\mid w_{t-n+1},\\ldots,w_{t-1})\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "| Model | Context | Example prediction |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Unigram | None | $P(\\text{growth})$ |\n",
    "| Bigram | One token | $P(\\text{growth}\\mid\\text{revenue})$ |\n",
    "| Trigram | Two tokens | $P(\\text{growth}\\mid\\text{strong revenue})$ |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Assumption:** tokens outside the fixed window do not affect the prediction.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Worked Example: Bigram Estimation\n",
    "\n",
    "Maximum-likelihood estimate:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat P(v\\mid u)=\\frac{c(u,v)}{\\sum_{v'}c(u,v')}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose “revenue” is followed by:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Next word | Count | Estimated probability |\n",
    "|---|---:|---:|\n",
    "| increased | 6 | 0.60 |\n",
    "| declined | 3 | 0.30 |\n",
    "| stabilized | 1 | 0.10 |\n",
    "\n",
    "An unseen continuation receives probability zero without smoothing.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## N-gram Features and N-gram Language Models\n",
    "\n",
    "| | N-gram features | N-gram language model |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Representation | Counts of token sequences | Conditional token probabilities |\n",
    "| Example | Feature for “not profitable” | $P(\\text{profitable}\\mid\\text{not})$ |\n",
    "| Typical use | Classification or retrieval | Sequence scoring or generation |\n",
    "\n",
    "Including bigrams in a document vector preserves some local phrase information, but does not by itself define a language model.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Sparsity and Smoothing\n",
    "\n",
    "- The number of possible n-grams grows rapidly with vocabulary size.\n",
    "- Many plausible sequences are absent from the training corpus.\n",
    "- Larger context windows require more data to estimate probabilities.\n",
    "\n",
    "One simple remedy is additive smoothing:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\hat P(v\\mid u)=\\frac{c(u,v)+\\alpha}{\\sum_{v'}c(u,v')+\\alpha V},\\qquad\\alpha>0\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Tradeoff:** smoothing assigns probability to unseen events but does not learn similarity between words.\n",
    "\n",
    "# Neural Word Representations\n",
    "\n",
    "## Neural Language Models\n",
    "\n",
    "A feedforward neural language model learns both word vectors and a next-word predictor. [@Bengio2003NeuralLM]\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Look up embeddings for the context words.\n",
    "2. Combine them into a context vector $x$.\n",
    "3. Compute a hidden representation: $h=\\tanh(W_1x+b_1)$.\n",
    "4. Predict: $P(w_t\\mid\\text{context})=\\operatorname{softmax}(W_2h+b_2)$.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Training objective:** minimize the negative log-probability of observed next words.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Embeddings: Learned Dense Vectors\n",
    "\n",
    "An embedding matrix $E\\in\\mathbb{R}^{V\\times k}$ assigns a vector to each vocabulary item, typically with $k\\ll V$.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Vector values are learned from a prediction objective.\n",
    "- Shared parameters allow information to transfer across contexts.\n",
    "- Similarity reflects patterns in the training corpus.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\operatorname{cosine}(u,v)=\\frac{u^\\top v}{\\lVert u\\rVert_2\\lVert v\\rVert_2}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "**Limitation:** static embeddings assign one vector to “bank” across its financial and geographic uses.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Word2Vec: Two Prediction Objectives\n",
    "\n",
    "Word2Vec learns static word embeddings from local context. [@Mikolov2013Efficient]\n",
    "\n",
    "| Architecture | Input | Prediction |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| CBOW | Surrounding words | Center word |\n",
    "| Skip-gram | Center word | Surrounding words |\n",
    "\n",
    "For “strong revenue growth,” with a context radius of one:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **CBOW:** {strong, growth} → revenue\n",
    "- **Skip-gram:** revenue → strong; revenue → growth\n",
    "\n",
    "These objectives learn word representations; neither is a full autoregressive generator.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Continuous Bag of Words (CBOW)\n",
    "\n",
    "Let $C_t$ be the available context positions around position $t$, excluding $t$.\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\bar v_t=\\frac{1}{|C_t|}\\sum_{j\\in C_t}v(w_j)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\max_{\\theta}\\sum_t\\log P_{\\theta}(w_t\\mid\\bar v_t)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- Aggregate context embeddings by averaging or summing.\n",
    "- Predict the center word from the aggregate.\n",
    "- Context aggregation discards order within the window.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Skip-gram\n",
    "\n",
    "Predict each surrounding word from the center word:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\max_{\\theta}\\sum_t\\sum_{j\\in C_t}\\log P_{\\theta}(w_j\\mid w_t)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- Each center word produces multiple center–context pairs.\n",
    "- The center position is excluded from its own context.\n",
    "- Each pair contributes a training signal to the embeddings.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Computation:** negative sampling provides an alternative training objective that avoids a full vocabulary softmax. [@Mikolov2013Word2Vec]\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## CBOW and Skip-gram Architectures\n",
    "\n",
    "::: {.columns}\n",
    "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "**CBOW: context → center**\n",
    "\n",
    "![CBOW architecture](./M01_lecture02_figures/cbow.svg){height=300 fig-alt=\"Context word inputs combined to predict a center word\"}\n",
    "\n",
    ":::\n",
    "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
    "\n",
    "**Skip-gram: center → context**\n",
