    "\n",
    "## Representation Choices\n",
    "\n",
    "| Representation | Encodes | Key limitation |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| BoW / TF-IDF | Term occurrence and weight | No order with unigram features |\n",
    "| N-gram features | Local token sequences | Sparse, limited context |\n",
    "| Static embeddings | Learned word-level associations | One vector per vocabulary item |\n",
    "| Contextual embeddings | Token meaning conditioned on context | Greater computational cost |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Selection criterion:** performance on the intended task, given data, interpretability, and computational constraints.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Applying the Pipeline in Module 1\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Define the task:** select the text unit and target label.\n",
    "2. **Prepare the data:** inspect extraction, cleaning, and tokenization.\n",
    "3. **Establish a baseline:** fit BoW or TF-IDF with a classifier.\n",
    "4. **Compare representations:** evaluate embeddings on the same split.\n",
    "5. **Inspect errors:** examine negation, boilerplate, and domain terminology.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Prevent leakage:** split documents before fitting vocabulary or IDF; use company or time grouping when the prediction task requires it.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## Summary\n",
    "\n",
    "- BoW maps documents to term-count vectors.\n",
    "- TF-IDF reweights counts using document frequency.\n",
    "- N-gram language models estimate probabilities from limited history.\n",
    "- Neural objectives learn dense vectors through shared parameters.\n",
    "- CBOW predicts a center word; Skip-gram predicts its context.\n",
    "- Representation quality must be evaluated on a defined task.\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "## From Static Embeddings to Generative Models\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dimension | Static word embeddings | Autoregressive contextual models |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Token representation | Fixed per vocabulary item | Depends on preceding context |\n",
    "| Training signal | Local context prediction | Next-token prediction |\n",
    "| Direct output | Word vectors | Next-token distribution |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Continuity:** both learn representations from prediction tasks; autoregressive models apply sequence probability to generate text token by token.\n",
    "\n",
